        "abstract": "Semiconductor devices can be used to generate and characterise ps pulses. A two-section semiconductor laser has been described which generates pulses of 20-30 ps duration at up to 16 GHz with a peak power of approximately 0.5 W. A two-photon absorption autocorrelator has been demonstrated, consisting of a reverse-biased p-i-n GaAs/AlGaAs waveguide. By measuring the two-photon generated photocurrent as a function of the time delay between the pulses in the waveguide, pulsewidth measurements of both a Nd/sup 3+/:YAG and a InP/InGaAs semiconductor laser have been made.<<ETX xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">&gt;</ETX>",
